Completion definition
The project is complete when a natural-language mission can be transformed into a validated task graph, tasks 
are assigned to suitable agents, agents navigate and execute in simulation, a system event triggers safe 
replanning, and repeated controlled experiments quantify performance against baselines. A generated 
notebook or one successful video alone is not sufficient.
