Project implementation guide | 6
Phase 0 - Convert the idea into an executable specification
Estimated focused effort: 2-4 focused hours
Goal
Remove ambiguity before coding by fixing the scenario, allowed actions, success criteria and safety rules.
Do this in order
1. Create a mission file with one natural-language mission, three named zones and a list of required outcomes. 
Define whether every zone requires visual inspection, an environmental reading or both.
2. Write down the allowed task types and the simulated effect of each one. Example: visual_inspection 
completes only when an agent with visual_inspection capability reaches the target zone and the inspection
operation returns a result.
3. Define agent capabilities, start nodes, initial battery, movement rate and permitted task types. At least one 
agent should lack a capability required by some task so eligibility constraints are genuinely tested.
4. Define mandatory versus optional tasks, task prerequisites, priority scale, task duration, energy 
consumption and what constitutes task success/failure.
5. Write measurable MVP acceptance conditions. At minimum: all mandatory tasks complete in the normal 
scenario; no invalid assignment is executed; no same-node or edge-swap collision occurs; one agent-failure
event triggers a replan; all metrics are traceable to logs.
6. Create a list of non-goals: no physical robots, no direct LLM motor commands, no learned low-level 
controller, no claim of formal physical safety certification.
Deliverable to create
spec/requirements.md, config/mission_demo.yaml and config/agents.yaml (or equivalent JSON files).
Exit gate - do not move on until this is true
The mission can be executed manually on paper from the defined task list. Every task has an unambiguous 
success condition, legal location, required capability and dependency list.
What to do next: Build the repository and runtime environment in Phase 1. Keep this specification as the 
source of truth when deciding whether to add features.
Phase 1 - Create the repository and reproducible Python 
environment
