Phase 2 - Define data contracts and task semantics
Estimated focused effort: 4-7 hours. Data contracts prevent components from silently disagreeing about what a 
task or agent means.
2.1 Separate plan data from runtime state
The LLM emits only a proposed TaskSpec. Runtime fields such as assigned agent, actual start time, actual result, 
current state and observed position are controlled by the coordinator/simulator and must never be trusted from
model output.
Candidate task schema
{
 "task_id": "inspect_zone_A_visual",
 "task_type": "visual_inspection",
 "target_zone": "A",
 "required_capabilities": ["visual_inspection"],
 "depends_on": [],
 "priority": 3,
 "estimated_duration_s": 30,
 "acceptance_criteria": ["inspection_result_recorded"],
 "retry_policy": "safe_to_retry"
}
Field rules
Field Validation rule
task_id Non-empty unique string; stable within a mission version.
task_type Exact member of an allowlist; no arbitrary operation names.

GENAI TASK PLANNING AND AUTONOMOUS COLLABORATION
Project implementation guide | 8
Field Validation rule
target_zone Must exist in the current world catalogue.
required_capabilities Non-empty or explicitly allowed empty list; every value from 
the capability allowlist.
depends_on List of existing task IDs; no self-reference and no cycles.
priority Integer in a documented range, for example 1 to 5.
estimated_duration_s Positive bounded number; treat it as an estimate, not a 
guarantee.
acceptance_criteria One or more recognized postconditions, not free-form 
executable instructions.
retry_policy One of a small enum such as safe_to_retry, verify_before_retry, 
no_automatic_retry.
2.2 Define agent and world schemas
Agent:
 agent_id: unique identifier
 capabilities: set of allowed capability strings
 current_node: valid world node
 battery: numeric value in [0, 100]
 battery_reserve: minimum battery required after a task/route
 status: IDLE | BUSY | FAILED | CHARGING
World:
 nodes: node IDs, including named target zones
 edges: endpoints, travel_cost, travel_time, energy_cost, blocked flag
 allowed_task_types: finite catalogue
 version: incremented when topology or policy changes
2.3 Define runtime task state transitions
Use a finite state machine so that illegal transitions can be rejected. A practical set is PENDING -> ASSIGNED -> 
READY -> EXECUTING -> SUCCEEDED. Failure states include FAILED and BLOCKED; retryable work may return 
to PENDING only through the replanning manager. A SUCCEEDED task must not silently revert to PENDING.
Transition Precondition / evidence
PENDING -> ASSIGNED Allocator returns a feasible eligible agent.
ASSIGNED -> READY All dependencies succeeded and the agent is available.
READY -> EXECUTING Safety monitor approves dispatch.
EXECUTING -> SUCCEEDED Executor returns and validates the task postcondition.
EXECUTING -> FAILED/BLOCKED Explicit failure event with reason and timestamp.
FAILED/BLOCKED -> PENDING Replanning manager confirms retry policy, current state and 
assignment feasibility.
2.4 Implement validators and unit tests
 Create schema validation tests for missing fields, wrong data types, illegal enum values, duplicate task IDs, 
unknown zones and unsupported capabilities.

