Phase 9 - Build automated regression and scenario evaluation
Estimated focused effort: 6-10 focused hours
Goal
Turn requirements into a reproducible experiment suite so every change can be checked objectively.
Do this in order
1. Automate all unit, component and integration tests. Use a mock LLM response for the continuous 
integration test suite so tests do not depend on a network or incur API cost.
2. Create the nominal and fault-injection scenarios listed in the evaluation section. Store every scenario 
configuration under version control.
3. Add assertions for key invariants: tasks never dispatch before dependencies succeed; assigned agents satisfy
capabilities; no forbidden move reaches simulator state; SUCCEEDED is terminal unless an explicit 
recovery design says otherwise.
4. Add a simulation runner that takes scenario ID, seed and variant as command-line arguments and writes 
one machine-readable result record plus detailed event logs.
5. Run paired experiments across variants A-D. Save the exact Git commit, dependency lock, config, seed and 
planner metadata with each run.
6. Generate metric tables automatically from logs. Manually spot-check a few records by tracing the raw event 
log to the computed aggregate.
7. When a test fails, reproduce it using the same seed/config and fix the underlying issue before rerunning the 
entire regression suite.
Deliverable to create
Automated test suite, scenario library, saved raw traces, machine-readable run summaries and metricgeneration scripts.
Exit gate - do not move on until this is true
The same deterministic run reproduces the same simulation result. The full regression suite passes. Invalid 
plans never execute. Metrics can be independently recomputed from raw logs.
What to do next: Create visualizations and a concise technical report in Phase 10.
Phase 10 - Produce the evaluation report and reproducible 
demo
Estimated focused effort: 4-8 focused hours
Goal
Communicate what was built, how it was tested, what improved, what failed and what remains unproven.
Do this in order
1. Generate plots for mission success rate, task-graph validity, makespan, distance/energy, allocation cost and 
replan recovery. Include confidence intervals where appropriate.

