2. Create a small timeline plot or event trace for one nominal run and one failure/recovery run. Show 
assignment, agent state, task states and the event that caused replanning.
3. Write a README with setup, configuration, execution commands, test commands, experiment commands 
and expected output files.
4. Write a report with problem definition, architecture, algorithms, experimental design, results, 
representative failures, limitations and future work.
5. Record a 3-5 minute demo: submit mission, show task graph, show eligible assignment, execute, inject a 
blocked edge or agent failure, show replanning and finish with metrics.
6. Freeze result tables after final tests. If code changes after the report, rerun affected tests and experiments 
and update the report.
Deliverable to create
Runnable demo, README, plots, report, saved configurations and a final results directory.
Exit gate - do not move on until this is true
A reader can reproduce the nominal run and at least one fault-recovery run from the README. Every 
reported number points to a saved run or aggregate file, and limitations are explicit.
What to do next: Use the final checklist at the end of this guide. Only then consider the optional ROS 2/Gazebo 
extension.

