Final completion checklist
 [ ] The project specification, agent capabilities, task types and acceptance criteria are version-controlled.
 [ ] The world and agent simulator runs without any external LLM call.
 [ ] Task schema and runtime task-state transitions are validated and tested.
 [ ] A manually authored mission completes end to end.
 [ ] Greedy and optimization allocators reject ineligible assignments and report infeasibility.
 [ ] The LLM produces candidate task graphs only; every candidate passes local schema and semantic checks 
before use.
 [ ] Every movement and task dispatch passes the deterministic SafetyMonitor.
 [ ] Fault events trigger replanning while preserving successful task results.
 [ ] Unit, component, integration and fault-injection tests pass.
 [ ] Experiment variants use the same scenario/seed set and saved configuration.
 [ ] Metrics are computed from logs and representative values can be traced to raw runs.
 [ ] README reproduces the demo; report includes limitations, failure cases and result interpretation.
 [ ] No API secret is committed, and no claim exceeds what the simulator or experiments establish.
Technical resources to consult while implementing
Use official documentation for exact API details because model/provider APIs and Python package interfaces can change. This guide 
defines the architecture and acceptance criteria; it is not tied to a particular commercial model provider.
 Python documentation: https://docs.python.org/3/
 Pydantic: https://docs.pydantic.dev/ (typed data validation)
 JSON Schema: https://json-schema.org/ (portable structural schemas)
 NetworkX: https://networkx.org/documentation/stable/ (graphs and path algorithms)
 SciPy optimization: https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/optimize.html (including mixed-integer linear 
programming interfaces)
 pytest: https://docs.pytest.org/ (automated testing)
 ROS 2 documentation: https://docs.ros.org/ (optional later integration)
 Gazebo documentation: https://gazebosim.org/docs/ (optional later simulation)

